      "artist": "Ken Lund from Reno, Nevada, USA",
      "description": "Mariposa County is a county in the U.S. state of California. As of the 2010 census, the population was 18,251. The county seat is Mariposa. It is located in the western foothills of the Sierra Nevada mountains, north of Fresno, east of Merced, and southeast of Stockton.\nThe county's eastern section is the central portion of Yosemite National Park.\nThere are no incorporated cities in Mariposa County; however, there are communities recognized as census-designated places for statistical purposes. It also has the distinction of having no permanent traffic lights anywhere in the county.\nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariposa_County,_California\n\nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Text_of_Creative_Commons_...",
